      "user": "I've decided on pre-cast blocks for my 420 sq. ft. backyard office.",
      "assistant": "Choosing pre-cast blocks is a great way to speed up your 420 sq. ft. backyard office build, as they arrive cured and are typically laid using a lime mortar with a short reference planning window of about 2 to 3 days before plaster sequencing. Because hemp-lime is non-load-bearing infill, remember that your design will still require a conventional structural frame (such as timber framing) to carry the roof, floor, wind, and seismic loads. \n\nBased on your project scale, a typical net exterior wall area often falls around 400 to 450 sq. ft. with a wall thickness of 10 to 12 inches, though exact volumes depend on your specific wall dimensions and thickness. \n\nWould you like to calculate the precise planning wall volume now by sharing your net wall area and preferred wall thickness in inches?",
